{"kind":"request","text":"AE-1 required pre-code act at exact main 5b342ee9c484c0c653dc1a363b852be83ef1d77b. CF-1 and CDF-1 are on main. Promise c359fc6d covers this proposal. No source edit, generation, compiler, test, build, install or deployment occurred. The IE-1 gate retains the executable slot.\n\nShared owner. Keep ArchiveDriver in packages/scope/src/archive-driver.ts. Make apps/room/archive.ts the one room deployment adapter, with a pure common policy builder in apps/room/archive-policy.ts. apps/room/worker.ts exports the shared DeployedScope subclass and composes its archive wiring over the existing scope Worker class. worker.grow.ts becomes a compatibility re-export of that same room entry; its class name, Durable Object namespace and migrations stay intact. No current Grow-specific directory, repository, release import or global policy cache chooses whether a room archives. Other exports and apps/room/fetch.ts keep their existing owners.\n\nTarget and read authority. Select a provider using the existing validated host readiness and installed-register policy. Reuse hostRegisterScopes (installed-registers.ts:20-24): absent INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES preserves the configured single root; an explicit bounded list must contain that root and agree with REGISTER_SCOPE. Discover each candidate's actual Directory through the checked genesis/creator chain, then require its recorded archive='journal' binding and the exact Directory/Destination repository agreement. archiveTarget already performs that route (archive-target.ts:65-180). Change archiveHostItem's one-directory configuration gate, not its proof duties: the Directory genesis/claim must come from an admitted register; verify retained founding claim, native cohort, destination birth and recorded host/namespace as today. A caller-supplied directory/ref or namespace RPC access alone grants no read authority. No setting names a directory or repository. A root that is not in the admitted register set fails closed.\n\nNative policies. Build the finite map from the existing reviewed platform archive catalog/data and version relations, including the Base family and the supported historical families. Do not turn platform() availability or equal declaration bytes into export permission. Native owners come from ownersOf over exact catalog data and runtime rules; capability support comes from CAPABILITY_CODE. Preserve exact pin/data/domain/max/place checks in archive-value-policy.ts and git/src/archive-policy.ts. A registry row is not blanket body permission: local and foreign inline classes still need complete metadata/privacy admission. Register, Membership and Inbox journals remain outside direct public export; any permitted retained copy keeps its exact existing consumer policy.\n\nInstalled package policies. First prove that this exact scope was created by the actual installed package, including ancestor chain, native Directory/Rules sibling relation, create request, job, root definition, release, semantic and presentation identities. Reuse/extract ApplicationActAdmission's immutable discovery (applications/act-admission.ts:120-211). Its current public API only returns allowed/revoked, so returning installation identity is a new bounded seam, not an existing API. Merely finding a digest in R2, an item slot or a retained under alias proves no installation.\n\nUse the Rules installation's retained canonical semantic and signed release proof as the primary archive source. The install already validates these values and exact declaration texts (platform/application-install-v2.ts:29-44). A new namespace-only, bounded proof read should follow applicationProjectionDeclaration's checked installation/retained-value pattern (application-projection-reader.ts:13-23; object.ts:868-877), but return the full proof needed for this archive and explicitly support the Base Rules pin. The existing projection method is insufficient and does not admit the Base pin. Verify exact release digest, signature/publisher, semantic identity, reachable declaration closure and canonical definition digests. Match the archived scope's pin against that verified closure and rebind its retained declaration bytes under the archive budget. Support v1/v2 only through their exact existing codecs; no parser fallback.\n\nThe normal full-packet source ApplicationContentStore.get(release) (applications/content.ts:23-44) may supply the same verified proof when needed, but is not a substitute for installation provenance. It bounds the private R2 read and readTrustedApplication rechecks the exact APPLICATION_TRUST publisher, host/capability support and definition digests. No Git/network refetch, compiled current declaration, package code execution or process-global cross-room trust cache supplies permission. Package signatures establish publisher identity; they do not supply owner tables, domain allowlists or archive permission. The runtime's reviewed closed policy builder supplies those permissions. Missing proof, unsupported cohort/domain or inconsistent digest refuses before archive payload selection.\n\nPolicy preparation must be asynchronous and charged: the current registry/admit boundary is synchronous before target resolution (archive-driver.ts:171-194), so add one bounded per-pass policy-preparation seam before export admission/provider work. Scheduling a candidate is not export admission. Recheck current trust and identity at use; preserve flight ownership until underlying proof work settles. Do not load all installations or add a discovery scan. The resulting per-pass policy snapshot contains only native catalog policy and the proven package closure. The static ARC-1 cost proof must include AE-1's actual preparation costs later; this proposal invents no overhead constant or free proof cache.\n\nExact Grow config removals. Remove vars.GROW_ARCHIVE_CONFIG in full: policy, release, directory and repositoryName. Remove wrangler.grow.jsonc's Text rule for **/*.dap.json once worker.grow.ts no longer imports the signed demo packet; that is its sole production consumer found by the source trace. Keep main='worker.grow.ts' as the compatibility entry. Keep ARTIFACTS and its namespace binding, ARTIFACTS_CONFIG, APPLICATION_CONTENT, APPLICATION_TRUST, APPLICATION_SCREEN_HOSTS, REGISTER_SCOPE/installed-root policy, creation pins, serving settings, observability and all class/migration names. Those still have independent owners. The archive's directory/repository selectors disappear; generic host/operator configuration does not. No replacement per-directory or per-release archive setting is proposed. ARCHIVE_RESTART_DIRECTIVE is not present in wrangler.grow.jsonc; keep its existing bounded internal recovery semantics if supplied, rather than turning it into discovery or policy authority.\n\nCompatibility. Keep ARTIFACTS_CONFIG's exact parser and installed-root agreement; remove Grow's extra hard-coded namespace/directory/repository/release restriction. Existing ArchiveRows retain their exact repository, scope/ref, confirmed/pending marks and retry semantics. If dynamic discovery selects another repository, retain the current target-different refusal; do not reset or silently retarget history. Preserve catalog distinctions between current Base and older supported room families, including private-source exceptions. The Grow regression must reconstruct its same exact signed installation policy from retained proof before its compiled packet/Text-rule path disappears. A missing legacy proof is a reported compatibility failure, not permission to use current maintained declarations.\n\nProvider decision needed. ArtifactsProvider.archive is a production host-owned port (artifacts-host.ts:194 onward). GitHubProvider has only fixtureArchive and explicitly no production archive mint (github-host.ts:82-91). Proposed AE-1 first shares the existing production Artifacts port across all room Workers; it does not silently promote GitHub fixture credentials. Please confirm whether AE-1's outcome is every Worker with a supported Artifacts archive binding, or whether AE-1 also owns a separately reviewed production GitHub archive mint/custody port. Unsupported provider configuration stays unavailable and visible, with no inferred credential authority.\n\nRevoked-release decision needed. Proposed default: current APPLICATION_TRUST remains required when constructing a package policy; removal stops new archive policy preparation and leaves existing confirmed coverage intact. If historical installed scopes must remain exportable after release revocation, please specify a distinct historical archive trust rule using their retained signed proof. Do not silently reuse installation-time trust or equate fresh-act admission with archive permission.\n\nPages, docs and witnesses. Derive host none from the room's recorded host and show 'No archive: this room has no repository.' Distinguish that from a supported host whose archive is unbound/unavailable; a missing receipt alone proves neither. Add 'Verify a room from its archive' to docs/operate-a-service.md with dap clone \u003cdir\u003e --archive, then artroom-replay --git \u003cclone\u003e --all --expect-journals N --json. N comes from an independently enumerated/proved expected scope set, not the fetched archive refs. The owning witness creates a non-Grow Base room, actually installs a signed package, binds its archive through the normal Directory act, archives and replays its clone. Keep the Grow answers; cover two directories without config selectors, installed-root compatibility, host none, policy/proof refusal and private journal exclusion. No restore or builder deployment.\n\nSecurity conclusion at pre-code review: the shared wiring can remove a single-room restriction without broadening payload authority if target proofs, current trust, closed native/runtime policy and complete privacy admission remain mandatory. The new internal proof read and production provider scope need explicit review; source inspection proves neither their implementation nor a new outside-effect model correspondence. Checker review must include the Security conclusion. AE-1 keeps existing archive caps and format. New ARC-1 ruling b188f9e7 replaces staging with an exact one-pass cohort and a permanent named pre-provider stop; that separate pre-code inventory/build follows AE-1. No staging, cap increase or universal archive guarantee enters AE-1.\n\nPlease accept or amend this proposal and decide the provider scope and revoked-release rule before production source.","body":{"conditions":"Accept or amend AE-1's pre-code proposal: shared driver location, signed installed-package policy authority, exact Grow settings removed, register/config compatibility, provider scope and revoked-release behavior. No production source or executable work before ruling. No ARC-1 staging or deployment.","no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b188f9e7e742f08ed16ee476f002a51d8412410a stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b5750e6e82650d29470d64f83b0dc3a50115b466","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}